# Ember.Proof.Z80LoopItems — the items of the loopback image, written out (plan M7.3)

`Loop.items` is what `Codegen.build` assembles for the loopback program
on the board, without the passes on the assembly (`passes := false`) and
without the trace: the board's cells and the layout as names, the reset
and interrupt vectors, the generated code, start-up, the routines of the
runtime the code uses.  Written out as a term so that the kernel can
assemble it; that it is what `build` gives is a `#guard` — evaluated
when this file is built, not proved.

